  "line": "Canaan is the land west of the Jordan that God promised to Abraham's family as an eternal possession, and it is where much of Israel's story takes place.",
  "moments": [
    {
      "title": "Abram Arrives in Canaan",
      "text": "Abram takes Sarai, Lot, and all their people and goods and sets out for Canaan. There the LORD appears and says He will give this land to Abram's offspring, and Abram builds an altar.",
      "passage": "Genesis 12:4-9"
    },
    {
      "title": "God Promises the Land",
      "text": "God makes His covenant with Abraham. He promises to give Abraham and his descendants all the land of Canaan as an eternal possession, and to be their God.",
      "passage": "Genesis 17:1-9"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sarah Dies in Canaan",
      "text": "Sarah dies in Hebron in the land of Canaan, and Abraham mourns and weeps for her. He then asks the Hittites for a burial site.",
      "passage": "Genesis 23:1-9"
    },
    {
      "title": "Spies Explore Canaan",
      "text": "Moses sends one leader from each tribe to spy out Canaan. They travel through the Negev and the hill country, and at the Valley of Eshcol they cut a huge cluster of grapes.",
      "passage": "Numbers 13:17-24"
    },
    {
      "title": "Manna Stops",
      "text": "At Gilgal, the Israelites keep the Passover and eat from the produce of the land. The day after, the manna stops, and that year they eat the crops of Canaan.",
      "passage": "Joshua 5:10-12"
    }
  ],
